public record LabClientProps(@NotBlank String baseUrl, Duration timeout, int retries) {}
Rule of thumb: more than two related keys means a @ConfigurationProperties record. Keep @Value for one-off values.

| @Cacheable | @CachePut | @CacheEvict
Method body runs | Only on a cache miss | Always | Always
Effect on cache | Stores the result on a miss | Overwrites the entry with the result | Removes the key, or all entries
Put it on | Reads: findById | Updates that return the new value | Deletes, or updates that do not return the value
Useful options | unless = "#result == null", sync = true | key = "#result.id" | allEntries = true, beforeInvocation = true
@Cacheable(cacheNames = "patient", key = "#id")
public Patient find(long id) { ... }
@CachePut(cacheNames = "patient", key = "#result.id")
public Patient update(Patient p) { ... }
@CacheEvict(cacheNames = "patient", key = "#id")
public void delete(long id) { ... }
Rule of thumb: never put @Cacheable and @CachePut on the same method. All three are proxy-based, so calls from inside the same class skip the cache.
